    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_f198405463cc27cbcffae255b00f301252223fbbda6eedd4539e0bfb3d98168d",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The span transfers between a zero exponential-sum representation and short-interval variation of the weighted coefficient error G_F, but the transfer is conditional and asymmetric rather than an exact equivalence. As theta_F increases, the exponent 1/(1/2+theta_F) decreases, so the cutoff T^{1/(1/2+theta_F)}/log^5 T moves to smaller x and cancellation is demanded farther down the x-range. Conceptually, the larger coefficient-growth allowance also enlarges the explicit-formula error O(x^{theta_F} log x), reducing the scale on which that bridge is informative. G_F gains a single arithmetic discrepancy coordinate by aggregating Lambda_F up to x and subtracting d_F x, while losing the identities of individual coefficients; RH_F, uniform conjectural cancellation, truncation control, and unequal forward/converse losses remain proof burdens.",
