    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2e0ee02d14243be7d021df1b1c9c112437c3ff3652ffaba996e192fd00f2b0ec",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The zero exponential sum is a common linear target reached through two genuinely different sufficient-information channels. The explicit-formula route cancels the constant prime error and reduces the sum to local differences G(y)-G(x), so short-interval prime regularity can control it. The pair-correlation route bounds the same linear mode by a quadratic energy, symmetrizes nearby multiplicative scales into a second difference of normalized pair correlation, and chooses beta to turn the strengthened uniform pair-correlation hypothesis into o(T) cancellation.",
