    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b936e00149c294aa7dae23b916609d5fbe05cd96133754dd106cf973bb41eaa2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The interval sandwich converts a sharp count into finitely many zero exponential sums; Landau's formula then acts as an arithmetic selector. When alpha is a rational prime-log multiple, exactly the q-divisible Fourier indices become prime powers and assemble into the g_alpha integral, while nonintegral modes are o(T). The remaining frequencies beyond J_0 isolate the separate proof burden rather than altering the resonant term.",
